// Plan 172.14 F.2 atom A2 -- forms probe for `sum_is_recursive`.
//
// Every declaration below pins ONE edge rule of the detector. The verdict is
// taken by RUNNING detect mode, never by reading the walk:
//
//   nova.exe check docs/plans/wip/172.14-f2-probes/a2-forms.nv   \
//     with NOVA_DETECT_SUMREC=1, then grep -E '\[a2-sumrec\] sum=F[A-Z]'
//
// Compare against a2-forms.expected; any drift is a detector change.
// Prelude sums are reported too, so the grep is anchored on `F` followed by an
// UPPERCASE letter: every subject here is named that way, while the prelude's
// own F-names (FloatKind, FmtKind) have a lowercase second letter and drop out.
//
// The pairs matter more than the individual rows: (FVec, FOpt) is the whole
// point of the atom. A `Vec` element sits behind a pointer and breaks a layout
// cycle, while `Option` is a by-value `NovaOpt_T` and does NOT -- so
// `type N enum Leaf | Node(Option[N])` must stay on the heap even though it
// "looks boxed". Likewise (FHeapRec, FValRec): the same shape through a heap
// record is finite, through a value record is not.

// (1) direct recursion
type FDirect enum DA(FDirect) | DB

// (2) mutual recursion through another sum
type FMutA enum MA(FMutB) | MAEnd
type FMutB enum MB(FMutA) | MBEnd

// (3) Vec breaks the cycle
type FVec enum VA(Vec[FVec]) | VB

// (4) slice breaks the cycle
type FSlice enum SA([]FSlice) | SB

// (5) str is a finite leaf
type FStr enum TA(str) | TB

// (6) Option[Self] does NOT break the cycle
type FOpt enum OA(Option[FOpt]) | OB

// (7) heap record is a pointer, breaks the cycle
type FHeapRec enum HA(HeapBox) | HB
type HeapBox { ro back FHeapRec }

// (8) value record is inline, does NOT break
type FValRec enum WA(ValBox) | WB
type ValBox value { ro back FValRec }

// (9) mutual through a value record and back
type FMutVal enum QA(QBox) | QB
type QBox value { ro q FMutVal }

// (10) raw pointer is indirection, breaks the cycle
type FPtr enum XA(*FPtr) | XB

// (11) fixed array is n inline copies, does NOT break
type FArr enum YA(YBox) | YB
type YBox value { ro cells [2]FArr }

// (12) no recursion at all, payload-less
type FPlain enum PA | PB | PC

fn main() {
    print("a2-forms")
}
